# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 4 and 8: the block is one binding group, so the door's first value is asked at the build with `$called`'s initial value, "front", the plain `let`s read the value `@Word "x"` ends on, and the count's label shows `$count`'s initial value; the holds and `@Word` take no position, so the places are the door, the labels and the buttons, in page order; the click on the bump button makes the count 11.
test a_build_reads_names_bound_below

tick 0
  added:
    0: Pad.Door(name="front")
    1: Ui.Label(text="door 1, hello x!")
    2: Ui.Button(label="never")
    3: Ui.Label(text="10")
    4: Ui.Button(label="bump")
  result: "door 1"

tick 1
  in:
    4: click
  changed:
    3: Ui.Label(text="11")
